title: Education & Science
new-page: true
is-card: true
view-if: kcp_in_government and chancellor_party = "KCP" and education_science_timer = 0
on-arrival: education_science_timer += 9; month_actions += 1
card-image: img/kcp_science.png
go-to: ed_menu
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet

# options:
# - fund research (basic science research at the KWI, medical research, applied and industrial research to benefit Germany's economy)
# - change the educational curriculum (only once per 3 years) - will have a "major" and "minor" option:
# - democratic education - focus on critical thinking and democratic values rather than authoritarian teaching. (+ democratization, pro_republic)
# - scientific education - focus on the sciences, mathematics, and technical skills (+ NMC, science)
# - humanistic education - focus on literature, history, and philosophy. (+ NMC, pro_republic if democratization is high)
# - traditional education (reduces relations with DDP)

# - increase educational opportunities for working-class families.
# - Secularize education (+ DVP, instant Zentrum vonc)

# source for some of the education stuff: Martin, G. W. “Educational Reform in Germany 1918-1933.” Masters, Durham University, 1972. https://etheses.dur.ac.uk/9738/.

# Forman, Paul. “The Financial Support and Political Alignment of Physicists in Weimar Germany.” Minerva 12, no. 1 (1974): 39–66.

# science increases economic growth...

= Education and Science

Education and science does not have any clear ministry and thus only through the power of the Primusship and goverment can we reform it.

[? if major_curriculum: Current educational curriculum - [+ major_curriculum +], [+ minor_curriculum +] ?]

@ed_menu
view-if: not last_advisor_action

- @increase_science
- @structure
- @curriculum
- @return: Do not enact any policies for now.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action


@increase_science
title: Increase funding for scientific research.
choose-if: finance_minister_party = "KCP"
unavailable-subtitle: This requires the Finance Ministry.

We finally have the funding and power to increase funding to our science teams. 

- @kwg
- @applied
- @medical
- @cut_funding
- @ed_menu: Do not increase research funding.
- @cancel_advisor_action

@kwg
title: Fund the remnants of the AUL.
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; science += 1; kwg_research += 1; economic_growth += 0.3 if economic_growth <= 8; new_middle_kcp += 5*(1-dissent); science_funding += 1

What remains of the AUL within Kaddu is demoralized and lacking funding. We can change that.

@applied
title: Fund applied research in economically useful technologies.
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; science += 1; applied_research += 1; economic_growth += 0.5 if economic_growth <= 8 and applied_research <= 1; economic_growth += 3 if applied_research > 1; new_middle_kcp += 5*(1-dissent); workers_kcp += 3*(1-dissent); up_relation += 5*(1-dissent); science_funding += 1

We fund economical studies.

@medical
title: Fund biomedical research at the hospitals and medical schools.
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; science += 1; medical_research += 1; economic_growth += 0.4 if economic_growth <= 8; new_middle_kcp += 5*(1-dissent); workers_kcp += 3*(1-dissent); up_relation += 5*(1-dissent); unemployed -= 0.2 if unemployed >= 4; science_funding += 1

Our research program focuses on medical research to improve the treatment of diseases and public health. [? if change_sex: Some of our medical advancements include new methods for sex change surgery and hormone therapy for transsexual individuals. ?]

@cut_funding
title: Cut science funding.
subtitle: +1 budget
choose-if: science_funding >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have not funded science.
on-arrival: budget += 1; science -= 1; science_funding -= 1; applied_research -= 0.33; kwg_research -= 0.33; medical_research -= 0.33; economic_growth -= 0.5; new_middle_kcp -= 5; workers_kcp -= 2; up_relation -= 5; unemployed += 0.3

We have cut funding for science. This has a negative effect on our economic growth, and unemployed scientists are less likely to support the SPD.


@structure
title: Change the structure and funding of education.

Education in Kaddu has often been governed by local goverments. This has lead with it becoming a entrenched defense of regionalism. This must change.

- @secularize
- @public_hs
- @ed_menu: Do not change school funding or organization.
- @cancel_advisor_action

@secularize
title: Support the removal of regionalist indoctrination in schools.
subtitle: -1 budget
unavailable-subtitle: -1 budget - requres a majority of parties to support secular schools.
choose-if: budget >= 1 and (kcp_r >= 50)
view-if: secularized = 0
on-arrival: secularized = 1; catholics_kcp -= 15; vnpf_relation -= 15; hp_relation -= 6*(1-dissent); up_relation += 6*(1-dissent); new_middle_kcp += 3*(1-dissent); workers_kcp += 3*(1-dissent); education_science += 0.5; new_middle_kcp += 4; new_middle_up += 4

@public_hs
title: Increase educational opportunities for the working class by funding public high schools.
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; public_hs += 1; workers_kcp += 6*(1-dissent); unemployed_kcp += 3*(1-dissent); prussian_police_loyalty += 0.04; education_science += 0.5; unemployed -= 0.2; economic_growth += 0.2; pro_republic += 4*(1-dissent);
max-visits: 3

# this makes the bureaucracy more proletarian
We have funded more public secondary schools so that impoverished children may receive the same education as middle and upper-class children, and can be prepared for universities.


@curriculum
title: Change the educational curriculum.
choose-if: curriculum_timer = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [? if curriculum_timer > 0 : It is too early to change the curriculum again. ?]

The current curriculum is too outdated for our modern state we must reform it! 

What should be the major focus of our new curriculum?

- @dem_major
- @science_major
- @human_major
- @vocational_major
- @trad_major
- @ed_menu: Do not change the curriculum now.
- @cancel_advisor_action

# note: education_science is a variable that affects how much education affects economic growth.

@dem_major
title: Democratic curriculum
subtitle: Critical thinking, democratic citizenship, and collaboration
on-arrival: curriculum_timer = 50; major_curriculum = "democratic"; pro_republic += 5*(1-dissent); workers_kcp += 3*(1-dissent); democratization += 1; education_science += 0.3
go-to: curriculum_minor

We should teach students how to be citizens of a democratic republic, by teaching them to critically evaluate politics and current events, to exercise their rights and to respect the rights of other citizens. Traditionalists of all stripes are critical of this curriculum.

@science_major
title: Scientific curriculum
subtitle: Modern science, mathematics, and technical skills
on-arrival: curriculum_timer = 50; major_curriculum = "scientific"; education_science += 1; up_relation += 4*(1-dissent); new_middle_kcp += 3*(1-dissent); workers_kcp += 2*(1-dissent)
go-to: curriculum_minor

Our educational system should reflect the modern age, and we should teach science and rational thinking. Religious conservatives tend to react negatively against this. 

@human_major
title: Humanist curriculum
subtitle: Arts, literature, history, and philosophy
on-arrival: curriculum_timer = 50; major_curriculum = "humanist"; up_relation += 3*(1-dissent); new_middle_kcp += 4*(1-dissent); education_science += 0.2
go-to: curriculum_minor

Our educational curriculum should be focused on the humanities, including arts, literature, history, and philosophy. Some criticize this curriculum as focusing too much on "useless" subjects, while others worry that the arts establishment is too closely tied to romantic nationalism.

@vocational_major
title: Vocational curriculum
subtitle: Useful technical skills for future careers
on-arrival: curriculum_timer = 50; major_curriculum = "vocational"; workers_kcp += 4*(1-dissent); rural_kcp += 2*(1-dissent); unemployed_kcp += 3*(1-dissent); new_middle_kcp -= 1; unemployed -= 0.1; education_science += 0.5
go-to: curriculum_minor

Education should be focused on providing a useful hands-on education, and teach the skills that will be most useful for students' future lives.


@trad_major
title: Traditional curriculum
subtitle: Classics, discipline, and nationalism
on-arrival: curriculum_timer = 50; major_curriculum = "traditional"; vnpf_relation += 5*(1-dissent); hp_relation += 4*(1-dissent); old_middle_kcp += 3*(1-dissent); rural_kcp += 3*(1-dissent); pacifism -= 1 if pacifism > 0; pro_republic -= 5; education_science += 0.2
go-to: curriculum_minor

The traditional curriculum had a focus on ancient history and language.


@curriculum_minor

And what should be a secondary focus of the curriculum?

- @dem_minor
- @science_minor
- @human_minor
- @vocational_minor
- @trad_minor

@dem_minor
title: Democratic curriculum
subtitle: Critical thinking, democratic citizenship, and collaboration
view-if: major_curriculum != "democratic"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "democratic"; pro_republic += 3*(1-dissent); workers_kcp += 2*(1-dissent); democratization += 1;

We should teach students how to be citizens of a democratic republic, by teaching them to critically evaluate politics and current events, to exercise their rights and to respect the rights of other citizens. Traditionalists of all stripes are critical of this curriculum.

@science_minor
title: Scientific curriculum
subtitle: Modern science, mathematics, and technical skills
view-if: major_curriculum != "scientific"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "scientific"; education_science += 0.5; new_middle_kcp += 2*(1-dissent); workers_kcp += 2*(1-dissent)

Our educational system should reflect the modern age, and we should teach science and rational thinking. Religious conservatives tend to react negatively against this. 

@human_minor
title: Humanist curriculum
subtitle: Arts, literature, history, and philosophy
view-if: major_curriculum != "humanist"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "humanist"; new_middle_kcp += 3*(1-dissent);

Our educational curriculum should be focused on the humanities, including arts, literature, history, and philosophy. Some criticize this curriculum as focusing too much on "useless" subjects, while others worry that the arts establishment is too closely tied to romantic nationalism.

@vocational_minor
title: Vocational curriculum
subtitle: Useful technical skills for future careers
view-if: major_curriculum != "vocational"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "vocational"; education_science += 0.3; workers_kcp += 3*(1-dissent); unemployed_kcp += 2*(1-dissent);

Education should be focused on providing a useful hands-on education, and teach the skills that will be most useful for students' future lives.


@trad_minor
title: Traditional curriculum
subtitle: Classics, discipline, and nationalism
view-if: major_curriculum != "traditional"
on-arrival: minor_curriculum = "traditional"; hp_relation += 2*(1-dissent); vnpf_relation += 2*(1-dissent); old_middle_kcp += 2*(1-dissent); rural_kcp += 2*(1-dissent); pro_republic -= 3

The traditional curriculum had a focus on ancient history and language.


